          "source_quote": "Quare ergo non interrogasti me de forma lapidum in structura repositorum, quod explevimus formas?",
          "english_quote": "Why, then, did you not ask me about the marks on the stones placed in the structure, and why we filled in those marks?[a]",
          "issue": "The added embedded question “why we filled in those marks” makes the reason for filling them an explicit subject of inquiry. The Latin explicitly asks why Hermas did not inquire; its quod clause states or explains the filling, rather than explicitly asking why the filling occurred. The English therefore introduces a causal question not expressed in the selected wording.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “Why, then, did you not ask me about the marks on the stones placed in the structure and about our filling in those marks?[a]” Review this proposal afresh against the Latin construction; if retaining an explicit question about the reason for filling, supply linguistic evidence for that interpretation.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
